# A2P2 visual style

The Canva home frame is the spec. After the intro overlay, the page is **navy `#20263e` with white type** — not the old light gray scaffold.

## Home (post-intro)

Stacked full-bleed bands, no cards, no hero overlay, no rounded photo:

1. **Header** — solid navy. Row 1: `HEADER_LOGO` + two-line tagline on the left; social icons + outline **Donate** on the right. Hairline, then row 2: left-aligned text nav (Our Story, Podcast, Programs & Pathways, Events, Get Involved, FAQ, Partnerships). Use `Header` from `src/components/Header.tsx` on every page — do not rebuild the chrome.
2. **Photo** — `HOME_PANEL` from `src/lib/media.ts`. Edge-to-edge, no padding, no radius.
3. **Who We Are** — heading, then white body on navy, wide measure, comfortable leading. CTA is a **line + arrow + “Learn More”**, not a filled button. It scrolls to `#mission`. The block unravels as it scrolls into view. No caption under the home photo.
4. **Our Mission + Our Principles** — same navy band, already on the page under Who We Are. Mission unravels as it scrolls into view. The Principles heading and numbered items (`01`–`06`) unravel as they scroll into view. Numbers are bold DM Sans at 33.2px in `#7199ab`, with `white/20` hairlines. Home ends here. Nav items are still separate routes (`/our-story`, `/podcast`, …).

## Chrome

- Site mark is `HEADER_LOGO` in `src/lib/media.ts`. Do not typeset `a²p²`.
- Donate is `border` + transparent fill. Socials are 20px white icons. Header type is 17px. Nav links are 17pt.
- Nav is plain text, no pills or underlines-at-rest.
- Logo bar scrolls away. Text nav is solid navy and sticky at the viewport top; no blur.

## Type and color

- Open Sauce One: wordmark, nav, buttons, UI.
- DM Sans: mission and long reading copy, 18pt.
- Tokens in `src/index.css`: `--color-bg` navy, `--color-fg` white. Do not reintroduce light `--color-surface` pages.
- Hairlines are `white/20`. Principle numbers use `#7199ab`; do not add other accent blues.

## Assets

Follow `media.mdc`. Home photo is LCP after the intro — `HOME_PANEL` is preloaded in `index.html`.
